explanation.text:
The failed run’s likely decisive error was its Nginx dev mapping: it combined an `alias` with `try_files $uri $uri/`, which can make `/dev/index.html` resolve incorrectly under the aliased directory and return 404 [T0B5:<RANGE>location /dev/ {
        alias /var/www/project/dev/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }</RANGE>]. The successful run used a straightforward alias plus `index index.html` instead [T1B3:<RANGE>location /dev/ {
        alias /var/www/deploy/dev/;
        index index.html;
    }</RANGE>], and that configuration passed the hidden tests [R1M.scores.reward]. The failed hook also unnecessarily ran recursive `chown` as the unprivileged Git user [T0B7:<RANGE>chown -R git:www-data "$target"</RANGE>] without adding that user to `www-data`, creating another possible hook error. Finally, it declared completion after only syntax-checking and reloading Nginx [T0B8:<RANGE>nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test is successful</RANGE>] rather than performing a test push and requesting both HTTPS URLs, so the bad dev routing was never detected.

The failed run used an incomplete locale warm-up: it constructed only the default locale and touched `ctype` and `num_put` before doing one `ostringstream` conversion [T0B26:<RANGE>std::locale loc;
        (void)std::use_facet<std::ctype<char>>(loc);
        (void)std::use_facet<std::num_put<char>>(loc);</RANGE>]. Although this happened to stop the observed executable from crashing and produced zero Valgrind errors [T0B28:<RANGE>ERROR SUMMARY: 0 errors from 0 contexts (suppressed: 0 from 0)</RANGE>], it did not robustly initialize all locale facets and paths used by the modified libstdc++. The successful run instead constructed the environment locale, explicitly initialized `ctype`, `num_put`, `num_get`, and `numpunct` [T1B18:<RANGE>std::locale loc("");
        (void)std::use_facet<std::ctype<char>>(loc);
        (void)std::use_facet<std::num_put<char>>(loc);
        (void)std::use_facet<std::num_get<char>>(loc);
        (void)std::use_facet<std::numpunct<char>>(loc);</RANGE>], and exercised `std::cout` locale installation before the custom heap was enabled [T1B18:<RANGE>auto previous_loc = std::cout.getloc();
        std::cout.imbue(loc);
        std::cout.flush();
        std::cout.imbue(previous_loc);</RANGE>]. Thus, the failed fix likely passed its narrow manual check but missed the fuller initialization required by hidden tests.
